# generated, and NOT committed: platform-specific build output.
# `/build/` is ANCHORED. A bare `build/` matches any directory of that
# name at any depth, and it silently swallowed src/std/build/ — the
# std.build module std.zen re-exports and example/build.zen imports.
# A stdlib module that is not in the repository breaks every clone,
# and git status does not show it, because it is working as told.
#
# `/zen` and `/zen-new` are ANCHORED FOR THE SAME REASON, and it is the
# same bug: a bare `zen` matched src/zen/, the CLI module PLAN.md's tree
# names, and swallowed it exactly as `build/` swallowed src/std/build/.
# Every name in this file that is a Makefile output at the repository
# root is anchored, because that is what it means.
grammar/zen.so
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.fixpoint/
/build/
.fixloop/
/zen
/zen-new
/zen-asan
/zen-fp
/tests/bench/out/
node_modules/

# grammar/src/parser.c IS committed — see docs/PLAN.md. Two generated
# files live in this tree, each named with the gate that proves it fresh:
#   seed/zen.c          <- the fixpoint
#   grammar/src/parser.c <- tree-sitter test
# Both exist so a user needs only a C compiler, never a toolchain.
zen-new.c

# gate.sh puts its private TMPDIR here, inside the worktree. Untracked and
# unignored, it was swept into a commit by `git add -A`: 548 node-compile-cache
# binaries against 5 real files, and nobody noticed until review.
.gate-tmp/
